      <section id="agreement">
        <h2><span class="num">1.</span>This agreement</h2>
        <p>This End User Licence Agreement ("agreement") is between you and <strong>SmartBuilders</strong> ("we", "us", "our"), which operates Business Executive ("the service"). If you register on behalf of a company, you confirm that you are authorised to accept this agreement for it, and "you" includes that company.</p>
        <p>By registering for or using the service, you agree to this agreement and to our <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, do not use the service.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="accounts">
        <h2><span class="num">2.</span>Your account</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>The service is for businesses. Each registration is reviewed, and we may approve or decline it at our discretion.</li>
          <li>The details you give us must be accurate, and you must keep them up to date.</li>
          <li>Keep your password private. You are responsible for anything done through your account, unless it results from our failure to protect it.</li>
          <li>Tell us straight away at <a href="mailto:info@smart-builders.co.za">info@smart-builders.co.za</a> if you think someone else has accessed your account.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="licence">
        <h2><span class="num">3.</span>Your licence</h2>
        <p>While your licence is active, we give you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable and revocable right to use the service for your own internal business purposes: connecting your accounting data and viewing reports on it.</p>
        <p>The software, design, dashboards and content of the service remain the property of SmartBuilders or its licensors. This agreement gives you no other rights to them.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="fees">
        <h2><span class="num">4.</span>Licence fees</h2>
        <p>Access to the service depends on an active, paid licence. We will agree the fee and licence period with you before your licence starts. When a licence expires or is not paid, access is suspended until it is renewed. Suspension does not delete your data; see <a href="#termination">Ending this agreement</a>.</p>
      </section>

